    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493338090/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Monday, May 4, 1908
We had an early lunch (Bernhard went to the Museo with Nora Ruffo), and went in the yacht round Ischia. Too beautiful for words. 
The Duke and Duchess Riario Sforza came to dinner. It seemed very dull, but Ethel said it was witty and brilliant for Naples! She herself is not a person who cares for conversation. She cares really for nothing but love-making. Of course she had Castel Maurigi to dine, and we left him with her. He looks very handsome. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 147 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1908> .

